  he moved to the u.s in the 50s widowed  27 years ago  he is now engaged to marry kathy this  summer  it was she who convinced him to return  to auschwitz  for closures he says world jewish  congress president  ronald louder says there's another  reason the survivors need to tell their  stories now  are you concerned at the rise of  anti-semitic incidents particularly over  the last few years  i'm very concerned about it because  when i look at what happened and i speak  to survivors  and they tell me how it started off very  small it got bigger and bigger and  bigger and bigger  is that what you're seeing i'm seeing  that same thing  the survivors numbers are dwindling few  think they'll ever be back to this place  all that will be left is the wire and  the watchtowers  and the ovens and their stories  mark phillips thank you thank you very  much mean it shows the capacity for  for recovery that human beings have yep  and so important for the stories to be  told i love the  the thinking that may we never forget  and that's why it's so important that we  keep telling it it's so amazing that he  that that man's been carrying that story  with him since he was 16  and he's now 91 and finally talking  about it  now because people are forgetting yeah
 

